Step 1 ✅ Connect ProjectModel to AnimeEditorController

Goal: AnimeEditorController owns a single ProjectModel.

After this step:

AnimeEditorController
        │
        ▼
   ProjectModel

Don't change any managers yet.

Step 2 ✅ Connect CanvasManager

Goal: Remove duplicate canvas data.

ProjectModel
     │
     ▼
CanvasManager

Instead of storing:

String ratio;
double width;
double height;

inside CanvasManager, it will use:

project.canvas
Step 3 ✅ Connect ClipController

Replace its internal list:

List<ClipModel> clips;

with

project.clips

Now all clips live inside the project.

Architecture:

ProjectModel
    │
    └── List<ClipModel>
Step 4 ✅ Connect FrameManager

Currently you have something like:

List<int> frames;

or

List<FrameModel> frames;

Move them into:

ProjectModel
   │
   └── ClipModel
           │
           └── frames

Now FrameManager edits:

project.currentClip.frames

instead of its own list.

Step 5 ✅ Connect CanvasPanel

Instead of:

canvasManager.ratio

it becomes:

project.canvas.ratio

The UI reads through the manager, but the data comes from the project.

Step 6 ✅ Connect BottomBar

Instead of:

frameManager.frames

the manager exposes:

project.currentClip.frames

No duplicate frame list.

Step 7 ✅ Save/Load

Now saving becomes:

project.toJson();

Loading becomes:

ProjectModel.fromJson(...)

No collecting data from different classes.

Step 8 ✅ Future Managers

Every future manager follows the same pattern:

ProjectModel
│
├── CanvasManager
├── FrameManager
├── ClipManager
├── LayerManager
├── AudioManager
├── ExportManager
└── HistoryManager

Each manager edits only its section of the project.
